{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773085899,"nonce":"l06gmUeT7IDqIB6M+cFXU0VuTJ4=","title":"Settings: dual-write reaper_* settings to config file for fail-closed enforcement","message":"The claude-reaper.sh script fetches settings from Mandible API at runtime. If Mandible is unreachable, curl fails silently and the script falls through to in-script defaults (all enabled). This means reaper_enabled=false has no effect when Mandible is down.\n\nFix: dual-write all reaper_* settings to ~/.config/claude-reaper/config (as shell variable assignments) whenever they are updated via PUT /api/settings/:key. The reaper already sources this file as a fallback, so the setting will be enforced even without Mandible.\n\nMapping:\n- reaper_enabled → CLAUDE_ENABLED + CODEX_ENABLED (both)\n- reaper_claude_idle_minutes → CLAUDE_IDLE_THRESHOLD_MINUTES\n- reaper_codex_idle_minutes → CODEX_IDLE_THRESHOLD_MINUTES\n- reaper_dry_run → DRY_RUN\n- reaper_cleanup_orphan_mcps → CLEANUP_ORPHAN_MCPS\n\nChange is entirely in src/routes/settings.ts (add a dualWriteReaperConf function, extend the PUT handler).","files":null}]}